%% Allocation lifecycle in the current Term (ASG): asg_allocation.status ACTIVE/ENDED/CANCELLED, refined by
%% code_released_at and resident_at; asg_allocation.end_reason says why it ended
stateDiagram-v2
  [*] --> AssignedUnpaid : assignment approved or Round-2 offer accepted (FR-ASG-03, FR-APP-07)
  AssignedUnpaid --> PaidWaiting : Balance claim confirmed (FR-BIL-03)
  AssignedUnpaid --> Cancelled : Balance not paid by its deadline or its claim rejected twice, forfeit (job, FR-ASG-11)
  AssignedUnpaid --> Cancelled : not enrolled, Bed released (FR-AUTH-08)
  PaidWaiting --> Cancelled : not enrolled, Bed released, payments refunded by rule (FR-AUTH-08)
  PaidWaiting --> Resident : check-in start reached and the Room's code confirmed (job, FR-ASG-04)
  PaidWaiting --> Resident : checked in at the desk (FR-ASG-04)
  Resident --> Ended : checked out, also after a termination (FR-ASG-06, FR-ASG-09)
  Resident --> Ended : moved to another Bed (FR-ASG-10)
  Resident --> Ended : the next Term starts for a continuing resident (job, FR-ASG-10)
  Cancelled --> [*]
  Ended --> [*]

  AssignedUnpaid : Assigned – unpaid (ACTIVE)
  PaidWaiting : Paid – waiting for the door code (ACTIVE)
  Resident : Resident (ACTIVE, resident_at set)
